---
description: Never add Co-authored-by trailers or claim commit authorship. Commits are the user's.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commits have one author: the user

Do not add `Co-authored-by:` (Cursor, an agent, or anyone else) to commit messages.

Do not set the git author or committer to an agent identity. Do not say in the message that you wrote or co-authored the commit.

If the environment injects a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer, strip it **before push** (`git commit --amend` of that unpublished HEAD only). Never rewrite already-pushed or tagged commits to clean this up unless the user explicitly asks.
